": {"input": 5467, "output": 422, "cacheRead": 47616, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 82, "totalTokens": 53505, "cost": {"input": 0.010934, "output": 0.005064, "cacheRead": 0.0095232, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.0255212}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1787745996908, "responseId": "resp_0190e2450c8980ae016a8ed6cd73c087d2bba07e4afccf4f28", "rawStopReason": "completed"}, "toolResults": [{"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_77pHae80VYkLWNn9eyEVDcgE|fc_0190e2450c8980ae016a8ed6d6b6d087d2b3bcff477c338bbc", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"classThreshold\": 15,\n  \"completedClasses\": [],\n  \"coordinate\": \"ant:ant:1.6\",\n  \"currentChunkClassCount\": 15,\n  \"exhaustedClasses\": [],\n  \"failedClasses\": [],\n  \"issueNumber\": 2392,\n  \"latestChunkBranch\": null,\n  \"latestChunkCommit\": null,\n  \"latestChunkPublicationId\": null,\n  \"latestChunkPullRequest\": null,\n  \"skippedClasses\": []\n}\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1787746007607}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_wz3BvNGOpR8TJrnVW0eeKZwC|fc_0190e2450c8980ae016a8ed6d6b6e087d2b02bd2163deaaa9b", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"rules\": [\n    {\n      \"excludeClasses\": \"**\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"includeClasses\": \"org.apache.tools.**\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1787746007607}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_VL8T7QIERiyVVYe7q10TMJYn|fc_0190e2450c8980ae016a8ed6d6b6e887d296bac5bcbfd505ce", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "# AR-build-infrastructure: Build infrastructure\n\nThe repository's build is a two-layer Gradle build, designed so that adding a\nlibrary never requires build-logic changes (§FS-repository-functional-spec.6) — coordinate discovery is\npurely metadata-driven. This document specifies how that build is wired; the\ntask surface it exposes is grouped in §TCK-test-harness, and the tests that\nprove the infrastructure works are in §E2E-infrastructure-tests.\n\n## 1. Harness layer (repository root)\n\n`settings.gradle` includes the build under `tests/tck-build-logic/`, which\npublishes the `org.graalvm.internal.tck-harness` convention plugin applied by\nthe root `build.gradle`. This layer owns the `-Pcoordinates=` filter, metadata,\nindex and stats validation, reporting, CI matrix generation, and packaging\n(§TCK-test-harness). It does not itself compile or run library tests; it\nresolves the selected coordinates and delegates each one to the per-coordinate\nlayer.\n\nThe harness resolves public library artifacts from Maven Central first. When a\ntarget artifact or transitive dependency is not present there, Gradle may fall\nthrough to the Confluent Maven repository at\n`https://packages.confluent.io/maven/`. Confluent publishes some artifacts and\ntheir transitive dependencies under non-`io.confluent` groups, so the fallback\nis intentionally available for any dependency after Maven Central is tried.\n\n## 2. Per-coordinate layer\n\nFor each selected coordinate the harness delegates to a separate Gradle build\nrooted at the coordinate's test project under `tests/src/<group>/<artifact>/<version>/`\n(§TESTS-suite). That project applies `org.graalvm.internal.tck`, built on\n`org.graalvm.internal.tck-base` and `org.graalvm.internal.tck-settings`, which\nwires the GraalVM native-build-tools plugin, the `javaTest`/`nativeTest` lanes,\nJaCoCo, and guards such as `checkTestTimeoutAnnotations`. Per-coordinate builds\nare isolated: one coordinate's outputs never affect another's (§FS-repository-functional-spec.6).\n\n## 3. Support library\n\n`tests/tck-test-support/` provides the `NativeImageSupport` helpers that test\ncode uses to assert native-image behavior. It is shared across all\nper-coordinate builds.\n\n## 4. Scaffolding\n\nTest-project and metadata templates live under\n`tck-build-logic/src/main/resources/scaffold/` — Java/Kotlin/Groovy/Scala test\nstubs, `build.gradle`, `settings.gradle`, `reachability-metadata.json`, and\n`user-code-filter.json`. The harness `scaffold` task instantiates them for a new\ncoordinate (§TCK-test-harness), so a contributor or Forge starts from a working\nproject rather than a blank directory.\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1787746007607}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_6DnczFUTCHk8B6JhhUTjnUwk|fc_0190e2450c8980ae016a8ed6d6b6ec87d296855e9a84d9833a", "toolName": "bash", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Compiled from \"AntClassLoader.java\"\npublic class org.apache.tools.ant.AntClassLoader extends java.lang.ClassLoader implements org.apache.tools.ant.BuildListener {\n  private static final int BUFFER_SIZE;\n  private static final int NUMBER_OF_STRINGS;\n  private java.util.Vector pathComponents;\n  private org.apache.tools.ant.Project project;\n  private boolean parentFirst;\n  private java.util.Vector systemPackages;\n  private java.util.Vector loaderPackages;\n  private boolean ignoreBase;\n  private java.lang.ClassLoader parent;\n  private java.util.Hashtable zipFiles;\n  private java.lang.ClassLoader savedContextLoader;\n  private boolean isContextLoaderSaved;\n  private static java.lang.reflect.Method getProtectionDomain;\n  private static java.lang.reflect.Method defineClassProtectionDomain;\n  static java.lang.Class class$java$lang$Class;\n  static java.lang.Class class$java$lang$String;\n  static java.lang.Class array$B;\n  static java.lang.Class class$java$lang$ClassLoader;\n  static java.lang.Class class$org$apache$tools$ant$AntClassLoader;\n  static java.lang.Class class$org$apache$tools$ant$Project;\n  public org.apache.tools.ant.AntClassLoader();\n  public org.apache.tools.ant.AntClassLoader(org.apache.tools.ant.Project, org.apache.tools.ant.types.Path);\n  public org.apache.tools.ant.AntClassLoader(java.lang.ClassLoader, org.apache.tools.ant.Project, org.apache.tools.ant.types.Path, boolean);\n  public org.apache.tools.ant.AntClassLoader(org.apache.tools.ant.Project, org.apache.tools.ant.types.Path